4.3 Rational Approximations

cf.expand = function(x, n = 5) {
    cf = numeric(n)
    for(i in 1:n){
        cf[i] = round(x)
        delta = x - cf[i]
        x = 1 / delta
    }
    cf
}
cf.expand(pi, 7)

[1]    3    7   16 -294    3   -4    5


continued fraction can be reduced to a simple ratio as follows Start with $ N = c_n $ and $ D = 1$. Then for $ i = n-11$ set \[
    T = N \
    N = N * c_i + D
    D = T
\]

rat.approx = function(x, n){
    cf = cf.expand(x, n)
    num = cf[n]
    den = 1
    if (n &gt; 1){
        for (j in (n - 1) : 1){
            tmp = num
            num = cf[j] * tmp + den
            den = tmp
        }
    }

    if (den &gt; 0){
        c(num, den)
    } else {
        c(-num, -den)
    }
}
rat.approx(pi, 1)

